WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Film Courage: How do you help clients who are&nbsp;
hyper-focused on other people’s achievements?

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.640
Erica Wernick, Personal Coach, Author and Speaker:&nbsp;
I help them get reacquainted with what their true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:14.960
dream is. I think it’s so easy to look at what&nbsp;
everybody else is doing and to decide that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:21.360
what success means and so that’s what I should go&nbsp;
after, but we really want to reconnect with what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:28.480
our true dream is. What is it that we truly&nbsp;
want? To tune out the noise, stop looking at what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.040
other people are doing, stop looking at social&nbsp;
media. What people are doing on social media,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:39.600
what they’re posting and really re-connect&nbsp;
to what is it that you truly want? I have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.840
this line in my book that I was actually really&nbsp;
proud of. I think it’s a good line where I said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.480
When you are trying to replicate someone else’s&nbsp;
magic, you are taking yourself out of the running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:56.080
for your own and I think that’s so important. I&nbsp;
think that as long as you are chasing somebody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.040
else’s dream or you’re trying to have or&nbsp;
do what other people are having and doing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:08.400
you are cutting yourself off from your own&nbsp;
fulfilling, really cool journey, really amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:14.080
magical experience you know it's going to be so&nbsp;
much more fulfilling if you reconnect to what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:20.800
it is that you want and go after it in a way that&nbsp;
feels good to you as opposed to comparing yourself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.200
to everybody else and trying to replicate&nbsp;
what other people are doing I think as long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:32.560
as you are trying to replicate somebody else's&nbsp;
path you're going to get stuck I think we all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.680
have our own path and we we need to find&nbsp;
our own path especially in an industry like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.800
Hollywood where there's no one way to do anything&nbsp;
you know if you lined up ten successful people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:48.240
or a hundred successful people and ask them how&nbsp;
did you break in or how did you get to where you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:54.080
are you're probably going to hear a hundred&nbsp;
different stories so it's important that we leave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.120
room for us to find our own story and that comes&nbsp;
from really letting go and disconnecting from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:05.360
what you see everybody else doing what's&nbsp;
your definition of a high achiever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:14.320
I that's such a good question because I use that&nbsp;
term all the time my definition of a high achiever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:23.600
is somebody who first of all has a desire for&nbsp;
something beyond like the base level you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:30.320
like people say oh I want to be a working actor&nbsp;
and i'm like really like that's such a base level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:34.240
thing I understand you want to pay your bills&nbsp;
from acting and sure that would be amazing but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.360
like that's one aren't you you're going to want so&nbsp;
many more things you know beyond that so I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:45.600
like number one it's about the desire the desire&nbsp;
for something greater than what's comfortable for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:52.720
most people and then I think that you know a lot&nbsp;
of my work in terms of helping people become high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:59.680
achievers is about how you think about what you're&nbsp;
doing what your belief system is behind what you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:07.440
are doing so that it leads to higher level risks&nbsp;
higher level actions and strategies that then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.120
usually lead to higher level opportunities&nbsp;
but so you know in my book I talk about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:19.760
10 pillars of the high achiever and it's it's&nbsp;
really about how you view what is possible and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.280
how you view what you're capable&nbsp;
of you know what you're able to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:33.440
so if you're a high achiever you view the world&nbsp;
in a way that you believe that anything's possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:41.280
and you make decisions based on your desires and&nbsp;
based on your dreams instead of based on fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:47.920
you know you do things that are not based on&nbsp;
those Hollywood rules you know you really go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.480
beyond what I call like the most people&nbsp;
pool so you're not doing what most people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:58.160
are doing you're doing what the smaller pool&nbsp;
of high achievers are doing which is you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:04.240
you're really you're really looking at the world&nbsp;
in a different way and and your own dreams in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:10.560
different way like if you have a dream of winning&nbsp;
an Oscar or being a millionaire you believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:17.600
that not only that it's possible but that it will&nbsp;
happen for you and just that belief changes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:23.280
it changes the entire trajectory you know of&nbsp;
what what potential you have in front of you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:31.040
so base level let's say filmmaker screenwriter&nbsp;
what would that would be they want to work on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:37.440
a few projects not they're looking to no I mean&nbsp;
like maybe my working actor example wasn't the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.840
greatest because i'm definitely not trying to&nbsp;
judge anybody's like level but I think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.920
you know like beyond student films beyond&nbsp;
unscripted you know if we're talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:52.640
Hollywood for for screenwriters or for any&nbsp;
other kind of craft you know I think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.640 --> 00:05:00.640
beyond what most people strive for you&nbsp;
know because I think that striving for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:06.480
like a base level keeps people safe&nbsp;
you know I think that most people that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:11.600
have dreams of succeeding in Hollywood in this&nbsp;
industry they have their dreams are beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:18.480
student films or their dreams are beyond you know&nbsp;
just paying their bills you know I think a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:24.480
people dream of telling really interesting stories&nbsp;
you know I think people love storytelling and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.640
art of storytelling you know a lot of the people&nbsp;
that I work with they want to make an impact on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.720
people's lives they want to make a difference in&nbsp;
the world through storytelling you know I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:38.320
that that goes beyond I just want to be able to&nbsp;
pay all my bills from my craft I think everybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:43.040
wants to be able to pay all the you know bills&nbsp;
from their craft but I think the high achievers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.520
they want more they want to they want to go beyond&nbsp;
that they don't want to stay safe and comfortable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:55.760
at whatever level is safe and comfortable what&nbsp;
are some of the achilles heels of a high achiever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:06.800
interesting question one of the things that I&nbsp;
personally have struggled with and I consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:14.560
myself a high achiever is all like the fact&nbsp;
that i'm kind of always reaching for something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:20.480
right and so I think that that might be an&nbsp;
achilles heel of the high achiever where that bar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:25.840
is always moving and and so that like one thing&nbsp;
that i've been working on is being more present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:31.760
you know being more present in where&nbsp;
I am and trying to enjoy the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:38.000
because my eyes are usually always on the next&nbsp;
thing you know i'm always reaching i'm always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.080
on that next thing I always want to know my next&nbsp;
goal you know right now i'm in this period where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:48.160
I don't really know for sure what that next goal&nbsp;
is for me and i've never experienced that before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:55.040
it's very uncomfortable to have to just sit here&nbsp;
and be present and wait for it to sort of come or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.040 --> 00:07:01.520
be inspired and so I think that's probably a high&nbsp;
achiever's achilles heels that you know they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.240
not really sometimes struggling with being&nbsp;
present and enjoying the journey and enjoying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:11.760
where they are because their eyes are always on&nbsp;
the next thing is there no other way around that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.680
as a high achiever is that just part of the&nbsp;
journey so to speak yeah I mean I don't I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:24.720
want to put my own struggles on anybody else and&nbsp;
make a blanket statement and say that you know all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:30.560
high achievers will you know struggle with that I&nbsp;
think everybody we all have our own stuff you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:37.920
so yeah I think you know everyone's going to&nbsp;
have their own struggles but it's really about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:57.840
how willing are you to do the work to better&nbsp;
yourself and to get where you want to go.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:02.374
Questions For The Viewers:

00:08:02.374 --> 00:08:06.640
How was this helpful to you?

